{"name":"Catskill White","hex":"#e0e4dc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Catskill (town), New York","blocks":[{"text":"Catskill is a town in the southeastern section of Greene County, New York, United States, and is the county seat of Greene County. The population was 11,298 at the 2020 census, the largest town in the county. The western part of the town is in the Catskill Park. The town contains a village, also called Catskill. The village of Catskill has a well-defined Main Street. There is a public boat launch on the Hudson River called Dutchman's Landing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Greene_County_NY_Catskill_town_highlighted.svg/330px-Greene_County_NY_Catskill_town_highlighted.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catskill_(town)%2C_New_York"},{"title":"Catskill (village), New York","blocks":[{"text":"Catskill is a village and county seat of Greene County, New York, United States. The population was 3,745 at the 2020 census, down from 4,081 at the 2010 census, down from 4,392 in 2000. The village is in the northeastern part of the town of Catskill."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/GreeneCountyCourtHouse.jpg/330px-GreeneCountyCourtHouse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catskill_(village)%2C_New_York"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1d/CatskillTownNY_seal.png/120px-CatskillTownNY_seal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1d/CatskillTownNY_seal.png/250px-CatskillTownNY_seal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1d/CatskillTownNY_seal.png/120px-CatskillTownNY_seal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACatskillTownNY_seal.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Cole_Thomas_View_on_the_Catskill_Early_Autumn_1837.jpg/250px-Cole_Thomas_View_on_the_Catskill_Early_Autumn_1837.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Cole_Thomas_View_on_the_Catskill_Early_Autumn_1837.jpg/500px-Cole_Thomas_View_on_the_Catskill_Early_Autumn_1837.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Cole_Thomas_View_on_the_Catskill_Early_Autumn_1837.jpg/250px-Cole_Thomas_View_on_the_Catskill_Early_Autumn_